"`#![inner_attribute]` applies to the enclosing [item](https://doc.rust-lang."
"org/stable/reference/items.html) (typically a module or a crate). In other "
"words, this attribute is interpreted as applying to the entire scope in "
"which it's placed. Here is an example where `#![allow(unused_variables)]` "
"applies to the whole crate (if placed in `main.rs`):"
msgstr "`#![inner_attribute]` applies to o enclosing [item](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/reference/items.html) (typically um módulo ou um crate). In other words, este attribute is interpreted as applying to o entire scope in which it's placed. Here is um example where `#![allow(unused_variables)]` applies to o whole crate (if placed in `main.rs`):"

