"In working with Rust, you will likely encounter methods that return the "
"`Result` type, such as the [`parse()`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/"
"primitive.str.html#method.parse) method. It might not always be possible to "
"parse a string into the other type, so `parse()` returns a `Result` "
"indicating possible failure."
msgstr "In working com Rust, you vai likely encounter métodos aquele retorna o `Result` tipo, such as o [`parse()`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.str.html#method.parse) método. It might not always be possible to parse um string no other tipo, so `parse()` retorna um `Result` indicating possible failure."

